ue of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids in Clarke County has a record from 1951 to 2025, and August to September came in under 90% of normal in 36 of those 75 years, more than any other pair of months. In 2025 the middle of the grids saw November to December at 38% of normal and August to September at 58%. So far in 2026, May to June came in at 211% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, with grid 14567 down at 55%.</p>"}
